abstract: >
  AMPidentifier 2.0 is a command-line tool for sequence-based identification
  of antimicrobial peptides (AMPs). It computes 22 physicochemical descriptors
  per sequence and classifies sequences using five independent classifiers
  (Random Forest, SVM, Gradient Boosting, XGBoost, LightGBM) combined in a
  soft-voting ensemble. On an independent benchmark set (n=4,736), the ensemble
  reaches AUC-ROC 0.950 and MCC 0.742.
